# Security Module

Production-ready security middleware and utilities for your Express.js application.

## Features

- **Rate Limiting** - Prevent abuse with IP and user-based rate limiting
- **CORS** - Flexible cross-origin resource sharing configuration
- **Security Headers** - Comprehensive security headers (HSTS, CSP, etc.)
- **Input Validation** - Zod-based validation schemas and sanitization
- **CSRF Protection** - Token-based CSRF protection
- **API Key Authentication** - Secure API key management with scopes

## Quick Start

### Basic Setup

```typescript
import express from 'express';
import { initializeSecurity } from './security';

const app = express();

// Initialize all security features with defaults
initializeSecurity({
  app,
  enableCors: true,
  enableRateLimit: true,
  enableSecurityHeaders: true,
  enableCsrf: true,
});

app.listen(3000);
```

### Environment-Specific Setup

```typescript
// Development (relaxed security)
import { devSecurity } from './security';
devSecurity(app);

// Production (strict security)
import { productionSecurity } from './security';
productionSecurity(app, process.env.REDIS_URL);

// API-only (no CSRF)
import { apiSecurity } from './security';
apiSecurity(app, ['https://app.example.com']);
```

## Individual Middleware Usage

### Rate Limiting

```typescript
import { rateLimit, createRateLimiter } from './security';

// Predefined configurations
app.post('/api/auth/login', createRateLimiter('auth'), loginHandler);
app.use('/api', createRateLimiter('api'));

// Custom configuration
app.use('/api/endpoint', rateLimit({
  windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000,
  maxRequests: 100,
  message: 'Too many requests',
}));

// Dynamic rate limiting by user tier
import { dynamicRateLimit } from './security';
app.use('/api', dynamicRateLimit({
  windowMs: 60 * 60 * 1000,
  maxRequests: 100, // Base limit, multiplied by tier
}));
```

### CORS

```typescript
import { cors, strictCors } from './security';

// Environment-based
import { environmentCors } from './security';
app.use(environmentCors());

// Strict (production)
app.use(strictCors(['https://example.com']));

// Custom
app.use(cors({
  origin: ['https://example.com'],
  credentials: true,
  methods: ['GET', 'POST'],
}));
```

### Security Headers

```typescript
import { securityHeaders, strictSecurityHeaders } from './security';

// Environment-based
import { environmentSecurityHeaders } from './security';
app.use(environmentSecurityHeaders());

// Custom CSP
import { mergeCSPDirectives, cspDirectives } from './security';
app.use(securityHeaders({
  csp: {
    directives: mergeCSPDirectives(
      cspDirectives.payment,
      { 'default-src': ["'self'"] }
    ),
  },
}));
```

### Input Validation

```typescript
import { validateData, signUpSchema, sanitizeHtml } from './security';

// Validate request data
app.post('/api/signup', async (req, res) => {
  const result = await validateData(signUpSchema, req.body);

  if (!result.success) {
    return res.status(400).json({
      error: 'Validation failed',
      errors: formatZodErrors(result.errors),
    });
  }

  // Use validated data
  const user = await createUser(result.data);
  res.json(user);
});

// Sanitize HTML
const safeContent = sanitizeHtml(userInput);

// Check password strength
import { calculatePasswordStrength } from './security';
const strength = calculatePasswordStrength(password); // 0-4
```

### CSRF Protection

```typescript
import { csrf, csrfToken } from './security';

// Enable CSRF
app.use(csrfToken()); // Generate tokens
app.use(csrf());      // Validate tokens

// In your template (EJS)
<form method="POST">
  <input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="<%= csrfToken %>">
</form>

// In client-side JavaScript
fetch('/api/endpoint', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: {
    'X-CSRF-Token': getCookie('csrf-token'),
  },
  body: JSON.stringify(data),
});

// Regenerate after login
import { regenerateCsrfToken } from './security';
await regenerateCsrfToken(req, res);
```

### API Key Authentication

```typescript
import { apiKeyAuth, requireScope, generateApiKey } from './security';

// Protect routes
app.use('/api/public', apiKeyAuth());

// Require specific permissions
app.get('/api/users',
  apiKeyAuth(),
  requireScope('users:read'),
  getUsersHandler
);

// Generate API key
const newKey = generateApiKey('sk'); // sk_abc123...
```

## Configuration

Create a `.env` file:

```bash
NODE_ENV=production

# Redis (optional but recommended)
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379

# CORS
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://example.com,https://app.example.com

# Sessions
SESSION_SECRET=your-secret-key-here
JWT_SECRET=your-jwt-secret-here

# CSP Reporting
CSP_REPORT_URI=https://your-domain.com/api/csp-report

# Email
EMAIL_FROM=noreply@yourdomain.com
```

